---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BlogCard from "../components/contentComponents/BlogCard.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../consts";

const recentPosts = (await getCollection("blog"))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf())
  .slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
  <aside>
    <h2 class="text-centered">Recent posts</h2>
    {recentPosts.map((post) => <BlogCard post={post} />)}
  </aside>
  <main>
    <p class="impact">Hello World!</p>
    <p>
      This is how it always seems to start. So it seems as good a way as any to
      start here.
    </p>
    <p>
      Perhaps that means nothing to you? Perhaps you have landed here without
      ever having seen a code snippet before. Perhaps you have never worked
      through the opening exercise of the latest coding or development tutorial?
    </p>
    <p class="impact extra-gap">No matter.</p>
    <p>
      For this is <u><b>not</b></u> a coding tutorial. It is a guide to some of the
      things that I have learned while trying to follow others' lessons and tutorials.
      And some other miscellaneous items that I also picked up along the way.
    </p>
    <p class="extra-gap">
      Hi, I'm Martin. I am a (relatively) new web developer but one with more
      than 30 years of other work experiences. I stopped doing the work that I
      used to do because I wanted to learn something new. And I promised myself
      that as I learned, I would keep a record of what I learned in case others
      might find them useful.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is what you are reading now - the introduction to some lessons
      learned. For example, this site is built on top of all the good work done
      by the team at <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>. A <b>big</b>
      thank you to them from me; I hope to share more on the subject of Astro builds
      once I have learned enough to share.
    </p>
    <p>
      My goal in writing the content on this site is to offer my "musings" on
      the world. The world of web developmet as I find it; and the world beyond.
      In writing, as in life, I view the world as I hope John Watson would have
      viewed it. John Watson, aka Wonko the Sane, is a character in the
      wonderful <b>trilogy</b> "The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy" that Douglas
      Adams wrote in
      <i>five</i> parts. If you haven't read it yet, then I highly recommend you do;
      it contains a lot of lessons for life. John Watson built an asylum against the
      whole world; he lived on the inside and was sane, everyone else lived on the
      outside and were not.
    </p>
    <p class="impact extra-gap">Hence I call this site "Sane Musings"</p>
    <p>The site is structured as follows:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/blog/">Blog content</a> where I attempt to capture and document
        what I have learned in building this and other sites
      </li>
      <li>
        Some thoughts on <a href="/wisdom">Wisdom</a> I have picked up along the way
        that I hope may help you along your way
      </li>
      <li>
        A <a href="/glossary">Glossary of Terms</a> to help navigate the content,
        the wider web and (in some cases) life in general
      </li>
      <li>
        And a list of <a href="/projects">Projects and other things</a> that I am
        working on.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Hopefully some of what you find here is of use and you may return looking
      for more as I build out more and more content.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .impact {
    width: 80%; /* size to whatever the text needs */
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    text-align: center;
    font-family: monospace;
    background-color: var(--color-table-highlight);
    color: var(--color-text);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .extra-gap {
    margin-top: 2em;
  }
</style>
